* LPUT - CREATE OR UPDATE A LIBRARY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* LPUT - CREATE OR UPDATE A LIBRARY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:LPUT [dir:]library [dir:]filespec[,filespec...] [+nn]

Adds or replaces library members, creating the LBR if necessary. +nn
specifies extra directory entries when supported by this version. Example
on copied files: SYSUTLS:LPUT I0:TEST I0:NOTE.TXT

Even a library-only invocation checks its format and updates CRC
information; it is not a read-only inspection command. Back up the entire
LBR first. Use LDIR for a directory listing.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
